From 767a46aa63b575af69c5b0d6ea16f8d634d0f170 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:37:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: for whoever is left alone a minimize and a hide are
 goings like any other

Two halves, and one of the two is minimized or its app hidden: the other leapt from its half to the whole display, and
back when the first returned. Nobody had named it. At a close, a float and a drag out it already stayed as it was.

Of the two places that everything consists of, with nothing left over, one is away (minimized, hidden, on another macOS
Space, in full screen): it keeps its room, and the Desktop stands in for it there. A rule of the layout
(`TreeView.leftOpen`): nothing in the tree changes, so that there and back is nothing.

Work in progress: the tests that assumed the old way are still to follow.
