+# Proposed by the executor of F68 (2026-10-15), from the product owner's ruling of that day; the documenter may edit or drop it.
+# Story: two halves. ⌘M and ⌘H are everyday acts that are not even addressed to Arbor, and name one window. The other is not named and does
+# not move: for whoever is left alone a minimize and a hide are goings like any other. What is freed is left over, and the one that
+# comes back takes its half again, with no frame on the other.
+# Reference: F68, T07; rules 2 and 3 of issue #3.
+quiet
+open Safari 900x600
+open Mail 900x600
+dock 101 left
+dock 102 right
+expect at 102 726 37 702x851
+# ⌘M in Safari, and back out of the Dock.
+minimize 101
+expect still 102
+expect at 102 726 37 702x851
+restore 101
+expect still 102
+expect at 101 12 37 702x851
+expect at 102 726 37 702x851
+# ⌘H in Mail, and back.
+hide Mail
+flush
+expect still 101
+expect at 101 12 37 702x851
+unhide Mail
+flush
+expect still 101
+expect at 102 726 37 702x851
+# What is freed is the Desktop: a place to go, beside the one that stays.
+minimize 101
+focus 102
+zoom 102
+neighbor left
+expect camera desktop
+show-all
+expect at 102 726 37 702x851
+# And what the pointer is seen on there, whoever has the keyboard.
+cursor 300 400
+in
+expect camera desktop
+show-all
+expect at 102 726 37 702x851
+# A gap dragged meanwhile is the hand's word: Safari comes back to what the hand left it.
+seam 0 -100
+expect size 102 802x851
+restore 101
+expect still 102
+expect size 101 602x851
+expect size 102 802x851
+seam 0 100
+# Closed while it is in the Dock: the one that stays never took the room, and stays as it is.
+minimize 101
+close 101
+expect still 102
+expect at 102 726 37 702x851
+close 102
+
+# A dock while one is away: on screen Notes takes the empty half, and Mail gets no frame. When Safari comes back: thirds, each moved once.
+open Safari 900x600
+open Mail 900x600
+open Notes 900x600
+dock 103 left
+dock 104 right
+minimize 103
+dock 105 left
+expect still 104
+expect at 105 12 37 702x851
+restore 103
+expect size 103 464x851
+expect size 104 464x851
+expect size 105 464x851
+# From three down the others share, as at a close: no hole among docked windows.
+minimize 103
+expect size 104 702x851
+expect size 105 702x851
+restore 103
+close 103
+close 104
+close 105
+
+# With a column for the Desktop: as before. Who is away lends its room to who is there.
+set desktopColumn true
+open Safari 900x600
+open Mail 900x600
+dock 106 left
+dock 107 right
+expect size 107 464x851
+minimize 106
+expect size 107 702x851
+restore 106
+expect size 107 464x851
